XXX revisit when our gtk4 supports dma-buf.
GTK implements GdkDmabufTexture only when built with <linux/dma-buf.h>
(HAVE_DMABUF = cc.has_header('linux/dma-buf.h') in gtk's meson.build), which is
not the case on OpenBSD: gdk_dmabuf_texture_builder_build() always fails with
"dmabuf support disabled at compile-time" and GDK advertises no dmabuf formats,
which since 2.54 also empties the negotiated buffer format list.  Negotiate
against the GL display and use the EGLImage import path (gdk_gl_texture_new)
when that is the case.

